References: <CAEe0rLRxLHD=SAVQbfyLKff9jYq7HiysQt1TGfhjc8o55DxaMQ@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <CANHDHZw1Pcx8Vudu2iiFXtD_sY7v7a_wbPPWexRAH3P=t_Hbmw@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Bowy, if you do exact matching, transformations like these won't have
any effect at all.  In the (more likely case) if approximate matching, the
issue is what is a good match.  So I would pick a matching method and see
what control units are matched to each treated unit. That's the ultimate
test here, and you'll understand the scale of your variables and whether a
log or the original units make the most sense.  Matching, viewed in this
way, is a sophisticated way of doing a simple thing.

Best of luck with your research,

Gary
